# System Diagrams

> Diagrams below use Mermaid, which GitHub renders automatically. Components shown are **proposed**, not a confirmed original inventory.

## 1. System Block Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    PSU["USB / 5 V supply"] --> MCU
    FS["Flame sensor module<br/>(analog out)"] --> MCU
    MQ["MQ-2 smoke/gas module<br/>(analog out)"] --> MCU
    BTN["Reset push-button"] --> MCU
    MCU["Arduino Uno<br/>filter, debounce,<br/>state machine"]
    MCU --> GLED["Green LED<br/>(normal)"]
    MCU --> RLED["Red LED<br/>(warning / alarm)"]
    MCU --> BZ["Buzzer<br/>(via NPN driver)"]
    MCU --> SUP["Simulated suppression<br/>amber LED / servo / low-voltage relay"]
    MCU --> LCD["Optional 16x2 I2C LCD"]
    MCU --> SER["Serial Monitor<br/>diagnostics"]
```

## 2. Control Flowchart

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Power on]) --> B["Lamp test<br/>init sensors and filters"]
    B --> C["MQ-2 warm-up<br/>(smoke channel ignored)"]
    C --> D["Sample sensors every 50 ms<br/>moving average"]
    D --> E{"Sensor fault?<br/>(stuck at extreme)"}
    E -- Yes --> F["FAULT state<br/>alternate LEDs, short beep"]
    E -- No --> G{"Flame condition<br/>debounced?"}
    F --> D
    G --> H{"Smoke condition<br/>debounced?"}
    H --> I{"Both active?"}
    I -- Yes --> L
    I -- No --> J{"Either active?"}
    J -- No --> K["NORMAL<br/>green LED on"]
    K --> D
    J -- Yes --> M["PRE-ALARM<br/>blink red, short beeps"]
    M --> N{"Persisted longer than<br/>escalation time?"}
    N -- No --> D
    N -- Yes --> L
    L["ALARM LATCHED<br/>red LED on, buzzer"] --> O["Pre-discharge delay"]
    O --> P["SIMULATED suppression ON<br/>for configured duration"]
    P --> Q["Suppression OFF (one-shot)<br/>alarm stays latched"]
    Q --> R{"Reset requested<br/>and conditions clear?"}
    R -- No --> Q
    R -- Yes --> K
```

## 3. State Diagram

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NORMAL
    NORMAL --> PRE_ALARM: one sensor confirmed
    PRE_ALARM --> NORMAL: condition clears
    PRE_ALARM --> ALARM: both sensors, or single sensor persists
    NORMAL --> ALARM: both sensors confirmed
    NORMAL --> FAULT: sensor reading stuck at extreme
    FAULT --> NORMAL: fault clears
    ALARM --> NORMAL: reset (button hold or 'r') and conditions clear
```

## 4. Output Truth Table

| State | Green LED | Red LED | Buzzer | Simulated suppression |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| NORMAL | On | Off | Off | Off |
| PRE-ALARM | Off | Blinking 1 Hz | Short beep each second | Off |
| ALARM (before delay) | Off | Steady | 300 ms on / 300 ms off | Off |
| ALARM (suppression active) | Off | Steady | Continuous | On for configured duration |
| ALARM (after one-shot) | Off | Steady | 300 ms on / 300 ms off | Off (latched) |
| FAULT | Alternating with red | Alternating with green | Short beep every 5 s | Off |
